# Ticketing System (TKT-001)

**Phase:** Full Production V1 design (documentation only; implementation tracked in §22 roadmap).

**Purpose:** Define the canonical **production-ready** contract for multi-tenant member support ticketing across Tour Ops clubs — domain model, lifecycle, authorization, API, UX, notifications, SLA, reporting, testing, and phased rollout.

**Principle:** Ticketing is a **platform capability** with **workspace-configurable** categories, queues, SLA, and enablement. Every read and write is **tenant-bound**, **backend-enforced**, and **fail-closed**. PostgreSQL + RLS is the only persistence path; memory storage is forbidden for ticketing data.

---

## 1. Purpose

**DECISION:** Clubs need a first-party support channel for members to ask questions, report registration/payment/profile issues, and track operator responses — without WhatsApp or external helpdesk tools in Full V1.

**FACT:** The platform already provides:

- Multi-tenant identity (`User`, `UserTenant`) — `apps/api/prisma/schema.prisma:537-564`
- JWT member sessions on Portal (PCMS-001) — `docs/standards/member-session-portal-authority.mdoc`
- Operator sessions on Web (`atour_op_session`) — same standard §1
- RLS via `withTenantRls` — `apps/api/src/db/with-tenant-rls.ts:16-39`
- CASL operator surfaces — `packages/workspace-sdk/src/auth/operator-surface.ts:6-17`
- Booking command-center inbox UX — `apps/web/src/features/bookings/bookings-command-center-shell.tsx`
- Portal `/me/*` BFF pattern — `apps/portal/app/api/me/wallet/route.ts:29-53`
- Wallet bounded context — `docs/architecture/adr/ADR-WALLET-001-member-wallet-bounded-context.mdoc`

**INFERENCE:** Ticketing reuses these primitives; it does not introduce a parallel auth or storage model.

---

## 2. Full Production V1 scope

### 2.1 Capability inventory

Legend: **V1** = Full Production V1 · **EXT** = Extension (post-V1)

| # | Capability | Tier | Actors | Permission summary | Tenant boundary |
| - | ---------- | ---- | ------ | ------------------ | --------------- |
| 1 | Create and manage tickets | **V1** | member, admin, owner | member own; operator tenant-wide | `tenantId` + RLS |
| 2 | Multi-message member ↔ operator conversation | **V1** | member, admin, owner | public messages; member own ticket | same tenant |
| 3 | Public reply and internal note | **V1** | member (public), admin/owner (both) | **viewer mutations = denied** | message `visibility` |
| 4 | Status lifecycle (§9) | **V1** | per matrix | core-enforced transitions | ticket `tenantId` |
| 5 | Priority triage | **V1** | admin, owner | member cannot set | ticket row |
| 6 | Workspace-configurable categories | **V1** | admin, owner configure; all read | manifest + `TicketCategory` | workspace + tenant |
| 7 | Tags and labeling | **V1** | admin, owner | filter/search | tenant-scoped tags |
| 8 | Queues and filtered views | **V1** | admin, owner, operator | saved filters + default queues | tenant |
| 9 | Assignment to operator or team | **V1** | admin, owner | `UserTenant` / team membership | assignee ∈ tenant |
| 10 | Viewer tenant-wide read-only | **V1** | viewer | **viewer = tenant-wide read-only**; **viewer requires tenant membership** | same tenant only |
| 11 | Secure attachments | **V1** | member upload on own ticket; operator read/write | signed URL + virus scan hook | storage key per tenant |
| 12 | Links to Tour, Registration, Payment, Wallet | **V1** | member create; operator read | FK validation under RLS | same tenant |
| 13 | Audit trail and activity timeline | **V1** | all read per role | `TicketEvent` + `AuditEvent` | tenant |
| 14 | Persistent in-app notifications (Portal) | **V1** | member, viewer (read) | Postgres outbox → inbox | tenant + user |
| 15 | Email and SMS abstraction | **V1** | system | provider port; no direct vendor in core | tenant config |
| 16 | SLA policy, business hours, escalation | **V1** | admin, owner configure | `TicketSlaState` persisted | tenant |
| 17 | Canned responses / reply templates | **V1** | admin, owner | `TicketTemplate` per workspace | tenant |
| 18 | Search, filter, sort, pagination | **V1** | operator; member own list | cursor pagination | tenant |
| 19 | Bulk actions (operator inbox) | **V1** | admin, owner | assign, status, priority batch | tenant |
| 20 | Reporting and management dashboard | **V1** | admin, owner | aggregate queries | tenant |
| 21 | Workspace ticketing settings UI | **V1** | owner, admin | categories, SLA, queues, templates | workspace manifest + DB |
| 22 | RTL, responsive, accessibility | **V1** | all surfaces | WCAG 2.2 AA target | — |
| 23 | Idempotency, concurrency, optimistic locking | **V1** | all mutators | `Idempotency-Key` + `rowVersion` | — |
| 24 | Observability, error tracking, retention | **V1** | platform | structured logs, metrics, retention jobs | tenant policy |

### 2.2 Per-capability delivery matrix (summary)

Each **V1** capability requires: domain rules (`ticketing-core`), persistence (Prisma + RLS), HTTP contracts, API routes, UI surface, events/notifications where applicable, automated tests, feature-flag rollout, and documented rollback (disable manifest flag → `TICKET_MODULE_DISABLED`).

Detailed phase mapping: §22.

### 2.3 Surfaces and actors

| Surface | App | Actors |
| ------- | --- | ------ |
| Member Portal | `apps/portal` | `member`, `viewer` |
| Operator Web | `apps/web` | `admin`, `owner` |
| Workspace settings | `apps/web` | `admin`, `owner` |
| Reports | `apps/web` | `admin`, `owner` |

**DECISION:** `viewer = tenant-wide read-only` · `member = own-ticket access` · **viewer requires tenant membership** · **viewer mutations = denied**.

