## 6. Tenant isolation and privacy

### Rules (MUST)

1. Every query includes `tenantId` from authenticated context — never from unvalidated body alone.
2. Every persistence call uses `withTenantRls(tenantId, …)`.
3. Never fetch by `ticketId` alone; always composite `(tenantId, id)`.
4. **member = own-ticket access** — `requesterUserId = auth.userId` on member routes.
5. **viewer = tenant-wide read-only** — no `requesterUserId` filter on list/read; **viewer requires tenant membership**.
6. **viewer mutations = denied** → `TICKET_VIEWER_READ_ONLY`.
7. `assigneeUserId` / team members must belong to same `tenantId`.
8. Related Tour, Registration, Payment, Wallet entities validated under RLS before link persist.
9. Memory driver MUST NOT implement ticketing repositories.

### Privacy

- Member never sees other members' tickets or internal notes.
- Viewer sees tenant tickets read-only including internal notes (audit/compliance role).
- Attachments: member sees own ticket files; operators see tenant ticket files; signed URLs short-lived.
- Retention: configurable per workspace (`workspaceTicketing.retentionDays`); default 7 years audit, 2 years attachments (configurable).

### IDOR mitigations

| Risk | Mitigation | Severity |
| ---- | ---------- | -------- |
| Cross-tenant read | RLS + auth.tenantId | P0 |
| Member reads another ticket | `requesterUserId` filter | P0 |
| Viewer without membership | `UserTenant` ACTIVE check | P0 |
| Viewer mutation | **viewer mutations = denied** | P0 |
| Internal note to member API | `visibility = public` filter | P0 |
| Attachment URL guessing | signed URL + tenant-scoped storage key | P0 |
| Cross-tenant assignee | team/user membership check | P1 |

---

## 7. Domain model (Full Production V1)

### 7.1 Model summary

| Model | Tier | tenantId | workspace scope | Notes |
| ----- | ---- | -------- | --------------- | ----- |
| `Ticket` | V1 | yes | via tenant registry | Core aggregate root |
| `TicketMessage` | V1 | yes | — | public \| internal |
| `TicketEvent` | V1 | yes | — | product timeline |
| `TicketAttachment` | V1 | yes | — | MinIO / receipt-proof pattern |
| `TicketCategory` | V1 | yes | `workspaceType` | DB + manifest sync |
| `TicketTag` | V1 | yes | optional workspace | many-to-many via `TicketTagAssignment` |
| `TicketQueue` | V1 | yes | per workspace | saved filter definition |
| `TicketTeam` | V1 | yes | — | operator group |
| `TicketTeamMember` | V1 | yes | — | join table |
| `TicketSlaPolicy` | V1 | yes | per workspace | targets + business hours |
| `TicketSlaState` | V1 | yes | — | per-ticket SLA clock |
| `TicketNotification` | V1 | yes | — | durable inbox row |
| `TicketTemplate` | V1 | yes | per workspace | canned responses |
| `TicketParticipant` | EXT | yes | — | watchers/CC |
| `AuditEvent` | V1 | yes | platform | existing compliance store |

### 7.2 Ticket

| Field | Type | Required | Notes |
| ----- | ---- | -------- | ----- |
| `id` | UUID | yes | PK |
| `tenantId` | UUID | yes | RLS key |
| `requesterUserId` | UUID | yes | FK → users |
| `assigneeUserId` | UUID | null | individual assignee |
| `assigneeTeamId` | UUID | null | team assignee (xor with user) |
| `queueId` | UUID | null | current queue placement |
| `categoryCode` | string(64) | yes | FK → TicketCategory.code |
| `priority` | enum | yes | low \| normal \| high \| urgent |
| `status` | enum | yes | §9 |
| `subject` | string(200) | yes | |
| `relatedTourId` | UUID | null | same-tenant tour |
| `relatedRegistrationId` | UUID | null | same-tenant registration |
| `relatedPaymentId` | UUID | null | optional payment link |
| `relatedWalletAccountId` | UUID | null | optional wallet link |
| `slaPolicyId` | UUID | null | FK → TicketSlaPolicy |
| `onHold` | boolean | yes | default false — operator pause (§9) |
| `onHoldReason` | string(500) | null | required when onHold |
| `lastActivityAt` | timestamptz | yes | |
| `resolvedAt` | timestamptz | null | |
| `closedAt` | timestamptz | null | |
| `archivedAt` | timestamptz | null | owner archive |
| `rowVersion` | int | yes | optimistic lock |
| `createdAt` / `updatedAt` | timestamptz | yes | |

**Indexes:** `(tenantId, status, lastActivityAt DESC)`, `(tenantId, requesterUserId, createdAt DESC)`, `(tenantId, assigneeUserId, status)`, `(tenantId, assigneeTeamId, status)`, `(tenantId, queueId, status)`, GIN full-text on `subject` (V1 search).

**RLS:** `tenant_id = current_setting('app.current_tenant_id')::uuid`

**Cascade:** messages/attachments/events cascade delete on ticket hard-delete (owner-only); archive is soft (`archivedAt`).

### 7.3 TicketMessage

| Field | Type | Notes |
| ----- | ---- | ----- |
| `id`, `tenantId`, `ticketId` | UUID | composite FK |
| `authorUserId` | UUID | from JWT |
| `visibility` | enum | public \| internal |
| `body` | text | max 10_000 |
| `templateId` | UUID | null — if created from canned response |
| `idempotencyKey` | string(128) | null, unique per ticket |
| `createdAt` | timestamptz | |

### 7.4 TicketAttachment

| Field | Type | Notes |
| ----- | ---- | ----- |
| `id`, `tenantId`, `ticketId`, `messageId` | UUID | optional message link |
| `storageKey` | string | `tickets/{tenantId}/{ticketId}/{uuid}/{safeName}` |
| `contentType` | string | jpeg, png, webp, pdf |
| `sizeBytes` | int | max 8 MiB |
| `uploadedByUserId` | UUID | |
| `scanStatus` | enum | pending \| clean \| rejected |
| `createdAt` | timestamptz | |

**Security:** pre-signed upload URL; download via short-lived signed GET; member only own ticket.

### 7.5 TicketCategory

| Field | Type | Notes |
| ----- | ---- | ----- |
| `tenantId`, `workspaceType` | | composite scope |
| `code` | string(64) | stable slug PK with tenantId |
| `labelKey` | string | i18n key |
| `enabled` | boolean | |
| `sortOrder` | int | |
| `defaultPriority` | enum | optional |

Manifest `workspaceTicketing.categories[]` seeds defaults; DB is runtime SoT after enablement.

### 7.6 TicketTag / TicketTagAssignment

`TicketTag`: `(tenantId, code)` unique, `label`, `colorToken`.

`TicketTagAssignment`: `(tenantId, ticketId, tagCode)` — index for filter.

### 7.7 TicketQueue

Saved filter: `{ name, filterJson, sort, isDefault, teamId? }` where `filterJson` holds status/priority/category/tag/assignee/unassigned/q.

Queues are **persisted views**, not separate ticket stores (JSM queue pattern — §21).

### 7.8 TicketTeam / TicketTeamMember

Team: `(tenantId, id, name, isDefault)`.

Members: `(tenantId, teamId, userId)` — all users must be ACTIVE `UserTenant`.

Assignment: ticket `assigneeTeamId` OR `assigneeUserId` (mutually exclusive).

### 7.9 TicketSlaPolicy / TicketSlaState

**Policy:** `firstResponseMinutes`, `resolutionMinutes`, `businessHoursJson`, `escalationSteps[]` (notify team, bump priority).

**State (per ticket):** `firstResponseDueAt`, `resolutionDueAt`, `firstRespondedAt`, `breachedAt`, `escalationLevel`, `pausedAt` (when `onHold`).

SLA clocks are **persisted**, not UI-only. Breach emits `TicketEvent` + `TicketNotification` + optional email/SMS.

### 7.10 TicketNotification

| Field | Notes |
| ----- | ----- |
| `userId`, `tenantId` | recipient |
| `ticketId`, `eventType` | deep link |
| `readAt` | null = unread |
| `payload` | JSON summary |

**DECISION:** Postgres-backed durable inbox (replaces in-memory member notification path for ticketing events).

### 7.11 TicketTemplate

`code`, `name`, `body`, `categoryCode?`, `visibility` (public reply vs internal), `enabled`, `workspaceType`.

### 7.12 Linked business entities

| Entity | Link field | Validation |
| ------ | ---------- | ---------- |
| Tour | `relatedTourId` | tour.tenantId = ticket.tenantId |
| Registration | `relatedRegistrationId` | registration.tenantId match |
| Payment | `relatedPaymentId` | finance module port |
| Wallet | `relatedWalletAccountId` | wallet ownership port |

UI shows deep links; no cross-module writes from ticketing.

### 7.13 TicketEvent vs AuditEvent

`TicketEvent` — product timeline (operator + sanitized member subset).

`AuditEvent` — compliance (`ticket.*` actions). Both tenant-scoped.

---

## 8. Status lifecycle and workflow

### 8.1 Status enum (Full V1)

| Status | Meaning | Label (fa) |
| ------ | ------- | ---------- |
| `open` | Active work | «باز» |
| `pending_member` | Waiting on member | «در انتظار پاسخ شما» |
| `resolved` | Soft close; member may reopen | «حل‌شده» |
| `closed` | Hard close for member | «بسته» |

### 8.2 Additional workflow concepts (not statuses)

| Concept | Tier | Representation | Rationale |
| ------- | ---- | -------------- | --------- |
| `reopened` | V1 | `TicketEvent` type `ticket.reopened` + transition to `open` | Avoids extra status; audit-friendly |
| `on_hold` | V1 | `Ticket.onHold` boolean + `onHoldReason` | Operator pause without inventing `on_hold` status; SLA clocks pause via `TicketSlaState.pausedAt` |
| `escalated` | V1 | `TicketSlaState.escalationLevel > 0` + event | Escalation is SLA-driven, not a status bucket |
| `awaiting_assignment` | V1 | Queue filter `assigneeUserId IS NULL AND assigneeTeamId IS NULL` | Unassigned is a queue view, not status |
| `new` | EXT | — | Redundant with `open` on create |
| `awaiting_operator` | EXT | — | Replaced by `open` + queue semantics |

**DECISION:** No new status literals beyond the four core values. Workflow richness comes from `onHold`, SLA state, queues, and events.

### 8.3 Transition matrix

| From \ To | open | pending_member | resolved | closed |
| --------- | ---- | -------------- | -------- | ------ |
| **open** | — | operator | operator | operator |
| **pending_member** | member, operator | — | operator | operator |
| **resolved** | member, operator | operator | — | operator |
| **closed** | operator, owner | — | — | — |

`onHold` blocks public member reply (409 `TICKET_ON_HOLD`) but operator may still update.

### 8.4 Concurrency and idempotency

| Scenario | Handling |
| -------- | -------- |
| Duplicate create/message | `Idempotency-Key` → `HttpIdempotencyRecord` |
| Concurrent PATCH | `rowVersion` → 409 `TICKET_VERSION_CONFLICT` |
| Bulk assign | per-ticket rowVersion or batch transaction with partial failure report |
| Message ordering | `createdAt ASC`, tie-break `id` |

---

