## 11. UI specification (Full V1)

### 11.1 Member Portal

| Route | Desktop | Mobile | RTL/a11y |
| ----- | ------- | ------ | -------- |
| `/me/tickets` | card list + filters | FAB create | chips with icon+text; focus order |
| `/me/tickets/new` | 640px form | sticky submit | `aria-invalid`, error summary |
| `/me/tickets/[id]` | timeline + composer | fixed composer | viewer: no composer, read-only banner |
| `/me/notifications` | ticket notification inbox | same | mark read, deep link |

### 11.2 Operator Web

| Route | Desktop | Mobile |
| ----- | ------- | ------ |
| `/tickets` | split-pane inbox + bulk toolbar | list → sheet detail |
| `/tickets/[id]` | timeline, sidebar links, SLA badge | full-page detail |
| `/tickets/queues` | queue manager | simplified list |
| `/settings/ticketing` | categories, tags, teams, SLA, templates tabs | accordion sections |
| `/reports/ticketing` | charts + export CSV | scrollable cards |

**WCAG 2.2 AA:** focus visible, status not color-only, keyboard bulk selection, screen reader labels on queues/filters.

---

## 12. Notifications and channels

| Channel | Tier | Trigger examples |
| ------- | ---- | ---------------- |
| In-app (Portal) | V1 | new reply, status change, SLA warning |
| Email | V1 | optional per workspace; template port |
| SMS | V1 | optional; high/urgent SLA breach only |

**Architecture:** ticketing emits domain events → outbox → `TicketNotification` writer + `EmailSmsPort` adapter. No vendor SDK in `ticketing-core`.

---

## 13. Observability and retention

| Concern | Full V1 approach |
| ------- | ---------------- |
| Structured logs | `tenantId`, `ticketId`, `actorUserId`, `traceId` |
| Metrics | `ticket_created_total`, `sla_breach_total`, `first_response_seconds` histogram |
| Error tracking | existing API error pipeline + `code` dimension |
| Retention | workspace policy: messages/attachments/events; audit longer |
| Rollback observability | feature flag off → metric `ticketing_disabled_total` |

---

## 14. Testing requirements

| Area | Tests |
| ---- | ----- |
| Contracts | `ticketing-http-contracts/test/*` |
| Core domain | lifecycle, permissions, SLA rules, onHold |
| Persistence | RLS, cross-tenant deny, FK links |
| API | per-endpoint HTTP specs, idempotency, rowVersion |
| Attachments | upload auth, scan reject |
| Notifications | outbox → inbox integration |
| Bulk | partial failure semantics |
| Portal E2E | member create → operator reply → member notification |
| Operator E2E | queue, assign team, SLA breach |
| a11y | axe on portal + web ticket routes |
| Fast-track | `pre-commit:fast`, `guard:import-boundary` |

---

## 15. Rollout and rollback (global)

1. Deploy schema + RLS with `workspaceTicketing.supported: false`.
2. Enable per workspace in manifest.
3. Portal/operator nav gated by entitlement + operator surfaces.
4. Sub-features (email, SMS) gated by workspace settings flags.

**Rollback:** manifest `supported: false` → API `TICKET_MODULE_DISABLED`; UI hides; data retained. No destructive schema rollback in production.

---

## 16. Risks

| ID | Risk | Mitigation |
| -- | ---- | ---------- |
| R1 | Memory driver hides RLS bugs | Forbid ticketing on memory |
| R2 | Viewer vs member confusion | Banners + permission tests |
| R3 | SLA clock timezone errors | business hours JSON + explicit TZ per tenant |
| R4 | Inbox perf at scale | indexes, cursor pagination, search GIN |
| R5 | Attachment malware | scan hook + content-type allowlist |
| R6 | Notification duplication | idempotent outbox consumers |
| R7 | Bulk partial failure UX | per-item error array in response |

---

